---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="What DataTales is, where the data comes from, and how every number is checked."
>
  <div class="container measure">
    <h1>About DataTales</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        DataTales turns UK public data into short, readable stories: what changed, who moved, and
        what stands out. It is written and run by {SITE.author}.
      </p>

      <h2>Where the data comes from</h2>
      <p>
        Stories use published datasets from official and open sources such as the Office for
        National Statistics. Each story links to its source and says when the data was fetched.
      </p>

      <h2>How the numbers are checked</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Every number is calculated by code from the source data, never typed in by hand.</li>
        <li>
          The raw file is stored untouched, with a checksum, and cleaned using a written, versioned
          recipe.
        </li>
        <li>
          Before a story is published, every figure in the text is checked automatically against the
          calculated values. A story with an unmatched number cannot be approved.
        </li>
        <li>A person reviews and approves every story before it goes live.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The “Source &amp; method” box at the end of each story shows the source, the fetch date and
        the cleaning recipe version.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        If you spot a mistake, please <a href="/contact">get in touch</a>. Corrections are made
        openly and the story’s “last updated” date changes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h1 {
    font-size: 2.4rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
  }
</style>
